    "context": "Context `shoal`. Namespace `compute` exists and is empty of your objects. DeviceClass `sgx-node` exists; its selector matches devices on the nodes. A device driver is installed; the scheduler allocates claims. No ResourceClaim or ResourceClaimTemplate exists.",
    "task": "Create Pod `tf` in `compute`, image `busybox:1.36`, command `sleep 3600`. The Pod must draw one device from class `sgx-node`, and its container must be given that device. You may either let a claim be created for it from a template, or create the claim yourself first and point the Pod at it. Do not request the device through labels or requests.cpu.",
